<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic calls snap elections after nearly two years of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac8dfab86b03889d62a7ccb2eb12ee0906758d3102852acb3d88faf37bf1e22f</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:15:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests--5f70b882a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic on Wednesday called snap parliamentary elections for October 25. They are expected to be a key test of his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iran attacks US base after American strikes on tankers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdc4aacb35688138843e184bfe252be5f55b924be3c47ad141e4f93b557fb804</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:43:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-iran-attacks-us-base-after-american-strikes-on-tankers--4a8c873638da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-iran-attacks-us-base-after-american-strikes-on-tankers" /><summary type="html">Iran said it fired ballistic missiles at a US base in Jordan early Wednesday, in retaliation for US strikes on Iranian oil tankers in the Gulf of Oman and near Kharg Island, off Iran’s coast. The US said five Iranian tankers were destroyed.</summary></entry><entry><title>'New escalation in Yemen deeply concerning everyone in the region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:473a4dd454a8edfb4169d3c1a471eed0bcdc30d6316209d400721c73ab35496d</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:39:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/new-escalation-in-yemen-deeply-concerning-everyone-in-the-region--833547815e7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/new-escalation-in-yemen-deeply-concerning-everyone-in-the-region" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Jules Grange Gastinel, Researcher at the Institute for Research and Studies on the Arab and Muslim World (IREMAM). He depicts Yemen as moving from a prolonged condition of unresolved conflict into renewed regional confrontation. The relative calm established after 2022, he argues, never amounted to a durable political settlement: Yemen remains divided between rival political, financial and military institutions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis report Saudi reprisals after oil sites set ablaze in wave of strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1957f3cf90d0e79f42b4689c7f1e072d775dc05b98574cf89402a563dd4f8e10</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:14:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-houthis-report-saudi-reprisals-after-oil-sites-set-ablaze-in-wave-of-strikes--6656793ba89e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-houthis-report-saudi-reprisals-after-oil-sites-set-ablaze-in-wave-of-strikes" /><summary type="html">The Houthis said Saudi Arabia retaliated with strikes on Tuesday after the group targeted oil facilities, wounding dozens, as deadly fighting reignited in Yemen after a Houthi offensive towards the Red Sea's Bab al-Mandab chokepoint. The rapid round of strikes and counter-strikes follows the unravelling of a four-year truce between the Houthis and the Saudi-backed government in July.</summary></entry><entry><title>War in the Middle East: Iran attacks US base in Jordan, 10 US vessels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:695f8107a3f666aada01e3678bb06b93db656155280f576a6e6feeaaa753306e</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:12:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-war-in-the-middle-east-iran-attacks-us-base-in-jordan-10-us-vessels--250d803900df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-war-in-the-middle-east-iran-attacks-us-base-in-jordan-10-us-vessels" /><summary type="html">Iran's Revolutionary Guards said Wednesday they pummelled a US military base in Jordan, vowing retaliation for American strikes on Iranian oil tankers that dragged the foes deeper into war. Tehran's bombs came after US forces destroyed five Iranian oil tankers on Tuesday in response to Iran targeting an American warship, the second such attack in less than a week. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran, Iran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Diplomatic row escalates as UK, France and Canada move to sanction Israeli settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4bcdbc51d0b3868f0ac9f3b996bb563ee6c28fbbdb4c006bdd77c1f002b89b3</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:10:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-diplomatic-row-escalates-as-uk-france-and-canada-move-to-sanction-israeli-settlements--b56444d3c0ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-diplomatic-row-escalates-as-uk-france-and-canada-move-to-sanction-israeli-settlements" /><summary type="html">Britain, France and Canada said Tuesday they will ban imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, with a UK minister accusing Israel of turning a blind eye to the "ethnic cleansing" of Palestinians there. The moves prompted a furious Israel to unveil immediate counter-measures targeting Britain, as Jerusalem-based journalist Jordana Miller reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>FRANCE 24 report reveals Russia’s war on Ukraine’s books and cultural identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ded9265f263ed6c20e703ba293c34838309f5a44e2802dff6f254460fa2c9dbf</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-france-24-report-reveals-russia-s-war-on-ukraine-s-books-and-cultural-identity--8e6f02fc74ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-france-24-report-reveals-russia-s-war-on-ukraine-s-books-and-cultural-identity" /><summary type="html">In Ukraine, the war is not being fought solely on the battlefield. This summer, Russian strikes severely affected the publishing industry, destroying dozens of warehouses and logistics centres. Millions of books and textbooks have been lost. For many Ukrainians, these attacks are part of an effort to erase their linguistic and cultural identity, as FRANCE 24’s Yegor Terletzkyi and Emmanuelle Chaze report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Albanian anger undiminished after 100 days of protests against Kushner project</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24986f8541b0855ed55470bb3ab05201f2676e0d6f45c538ef619e7f70fc13f0</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-albanian-anger-undiminished-after-100-days-of-protests-against-kushner-project--32214e2eaf06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-albanian-anger-undiminished-after-100-days-of-protests-against-kushner-project" /><summary type="html">Police in Albania blocked protesters from reaching parliament on Tuesday at the latest rally against a luxury development linked to US President Donald Trump’s son-in-law, Jared Kushner. Dubbed the ‘flamingo revolution’ for protesters’ signs depicting the pink bird that could be harmed by the coastal development, the protests are aimed at stopping the massive project that critics say would cause environmental damage and limit public access to the coast.</summary></entry><entry><title>How France fell in love with Céline Dion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f8af58f12ef8af6e8cb57f92e1684304d2fe4336a6cdeeca4d09dd56cbb0b67</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:07:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260909-how-france-fell-in-love-with-c_line-dion--a816cc5cdea2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260909-how-france-fell-in-love-with-c%C3%A9line-dion" /><summary type="html">Two years after her dazzling performance atop the Eiffel Tower for the 2024 Olympic Games in Paris, Céline Dion is back in the French capital for a series of sold-out concerts – and fans are over the moon. Some 500,000 people are expected to attend the concerts.</summary><category term="France in focus" /></entry><entry><title>US Rubio pledges to 'restore' ties with Colombia's new, Trump-friendly leader</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d1c1d28ca8683dfa3a6cd7b80abb507977d7b7663dc98ee5c4f471d1e4c2c13</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:05:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-us-rubio-pledges-to-restore-ties-with-colombia-s-new-trump-friendly-leader--1ac552445e85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-us-rubio-pledges-to-restore-ties-with-colombia-s-new-trump-friendly-leader" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday pledged to "restore" ties with Bogota after four years of leftist rule, on day one of a three-nation tour aimed at bolstering conservative allies in Latin America. The trip to Colombia, Ecuador and Peru comes after a series of elections brought pro-US right-wing leaders to power, giving Washington an opening to tighten security and economic ties and push back against China's growing influence. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ballon d'Or: Dembélé, Kane and Mbappé among shortlisted stars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62c5adb623c7a9b4c7a3ee82c3a26e15b17e8e68d44c8a78774473a66e2d0244</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:03:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-ballon-d-or-demb_l_-kane-and-mbapp_-among-shortlisted-stars--006d599f0b16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-ballon-d-or-demb%C3%A9l%C3%A9-kane-and-mbapp%C3%A9-among-shortlisted-stars" /><summary type="html">Ousmane Dembélé, Harry Kane and Kylian Mbappé are among the top contenders for the men’s Ballon d’Or. The 30 men’s and 30 women’s nominees were revealed by France Football magazine on Tuesday, with the winners to be announced at a ceremony in London on October 26.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hormuz impasse deepens: Iran retaliates against US targets after its oil tankers destroyed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db7232ebc6f4b7d892a23bd01dead8475a2d3055c7682734f17f0dbe0a444bcc</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:02:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-hormuz-impasse-deepens-iran-retaliates-against-us-targets-after-its-oil-tankers-destroyed--c25387f0269e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260909-hormuz-impasse-deepens-iran-retaliates-against-us-targets-after-its-oil-tankers-destroyed" /><summary type="html">Iran launched fresh attacks against US targets in the Middle East on Wednesday in retaliation for American strikes on Iranian oil tankers, dragging the foes deeper into war. Tehran's powerful Revolutionary Guards said Wednesday they attacked 20 US vessels trying to pass through the Strait of Hormuz, a vital waterway for the world's oil and gas that Iran has largely controlled since the war erupted. The United States and Iran are locked in a stalemate six months into the war, with Iran maintaining a stranglehold on the Strait of Hormuz and Washington pushing a campaign to choke Iran's ports and economy.</summary></entry><entry><title>JNIM jihadists step up incursions into northern Benin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cf796b40b6eafc95495371cc7e3964562a1afc04b5b4fa1b21066334fac28ff</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:00:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260909-jnim-jihadists-step-up-incursions-northern-benin--c61528c3ec0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260909-jnim-jihadists-step-up-incursions-northern-benin" /><summary type="html">Al Qaeda affiliate JNIM has been intensifying its activities in Benin since 2022. The country serves as a transit corridor between the areas of operation of the group, which is well established in Mali, Niger and Burkina Faso. Two nature reserves have become logistical hubs for the jihadist fighters. Benin's army is striving to hold the line.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strike near Ukraine-Moldova border kills at least two as Ukraine targets oil terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8eef9d3ca8db9c7fc45488a429b6bc238c6bd712cc582692bdb65ac659ac9055</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:51:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-ter--fc9e4da4f8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-terminal" /><summary type="html">An overnight Russian drone strike at a border crossing between Ukraine and Moldova killed at least two people, Odesa's regional governor said Wednesday. Moldovan Prime Minister Vasile Tofan said that 17 drones had hit Moldovan territory in August alone as both Kyiv and Moscow ramp up long-range strikes on military and energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>European space sector in the spotlight as Paris hosts International Space Summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fca53a0f2be0d6df202715bad94d30c98fc3201479e18ea39ef089d663c37000</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:17:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260909-european-space-sector-in-the-spotlight-as-paris-hosts-international-space-summit--759aa19da806.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260909-european-space-sector-in-the-spotlight-as-paris-hosts-international-space-summit" /><summary type="html">Paris's Grand Palais will host a two-day International Space Summit this Wednesday to promote global cooperation in the sector. A number of deals and investments for European space firms are expected to be announced as part of a wider plan to strengthen Europe's position in a field dominated by the US and China. Also in this edition: the US and Canada are locked in a tit-for-tat battle over tariffs.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why is France so good at animation?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b63c84c53e2cddcf0fd5afb92c9c738126fe857cf4f6bc11dad1617359e0c0a</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:14:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/why-is-france-so-good-at-animation--0717ddbd6b5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/why-is-france-so-good-at-animation" /><summary type="html">🇫🇷 🎞️ Usually associated with high fashion and culinary excellence, the French touch is prominent in another field not many know about: animation. The French animation industry is the third-largest exporter of animated content in the world, behind only the US and Japan.
 
But why is France so good at animation? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI says its models solved one of math's hardest problems as researchers cry foul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bfc4ea862b8eb1621cb892c53530c7e71f86e966fd6f0822265e34c4ada33e4</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:29:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20260909-openai-says-models-solved-one-of-math-hardest-problems-researchers-cry-foul--ab828afd1c78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260909-openai-says-models-solved-one-of-math-hardest-problems-researchers-cry-foul" /><summary type="html">US tech giant OpenAI on Tuesday said it had solved one of the hardest problems in mathematics with an unreleased artificial intelligence model after just 88 hours – and millions of dollars' worth of computing power. But a US mathematician and a researcher at rival Anthropic allege that OpenAI only took up the problem after it had gotten wind of their own AI-assisted efforts to crack the challenge which had demanded months to craft a radically distinctive approach.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower row over Hindu sect BAPS unites French politicians – but divides Indian diaspora</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83213eb7cfb36645a5edea17327e4ef22b6751c581c33bc329c5b3de70ab9210</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T06:37:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-eiffel-tower-row-over-hindu-sect-baps-unites-french-politicians-_-but-divides-indian-diaspo--84c7c8ecd3d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260909-eiffel-tower-row-over-hindu-sect-baps-unites-french-politicians-%E2%80%93-but-divides-indian-diaspora" /><summary type="html">France got a crash course on the Bochasanwasi Akshar Purushottam Swaminarayan Sanstha (BAPS), a Hindu sect at the heart of an Eiffel Tower strike this week. But for Indians in France who have been trying to raise awareness of far-right Hindu groups, it comes too late. As the 2027 election campaign goes into high gear, some fear the issue will be politicised by the French far right.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio hails Colombia's new pro-Trump leader De la Espriella on first stop of Latin American tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51a41f9a44a7026ff74a50b4b385b7b30e05c08b91983b62faae9d79e11aef62</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T06:27:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-hails-colombia-new-pro-trump-leader-de-la-espriella-first-stop-of-latin-american-tour--5ea929df5bfe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-rubio-hails-colombia-new-pro-trump-leader-de-la-espriella-first-stop-of-latin-american-tour" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio pledged closer security cooperation with Bogota on the first stop of his three-nation tour of pro-Washington Latin American nations. Rubio hailed the election of Colombian President Abelardo De La Espriella as part of a growing alignment with US interests across the Western Hemisphere.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Champions League: Madrid and Mbappé defeat Inter despite defensive lapses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84687198890c6c1556555b4da625a853d572a0565d4eb07f4c54e54750e9a7dd</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:45:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260909-champions-league-madrid-and-mbapp_-defeat-inter-despite-defensive-lapses--f45068f05b40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260909-champions-league-madrid-and-mbapp%C3%A9-defeat-inter-despite-defensive-lapses" /><summary type="html">Real Madrid won the headline clash of the first night of the Champions League against Inter (2-1). Kylian Mbappé, who kicked the first goal in, is now the fifth-highest scorer in the competition’s history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Travellers in UK face ongoing disruption after air traffic control glitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:044543aa0f1c1fa71f4cc6745a2cfc7d7c382baf28a1c68da363c0c6a4c72904</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T03:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch--92d15f16fe8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch" /><summary type="html">Flights from British airports began to resume Wednesday after a glitch in the country's air traffic control service left hundreds of thousands of passengers stranded. Authorities warned that travellers would continue to experience delays as airlines scrambled to recover from the outage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US bans Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as trade spat escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5090219c28e30edf2fc43b4959293ecab722e4fd4abb97d0986f060e44d6e150</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T02:36:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates--c7ae8aea47d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-us-bans-canadian-alcohol-motorcycles-and-dairy-products-as-trade-spat-escalates" /><summary type="html">The US and Canada escalated a bitter trade dispute on Tuesday, with Washington imposing new import bans on Canadian alcohol, motorcycles and dairy products as Ottawa's retaliatory tariffs on US goods took effect.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>New York City releases post-9/11 air toxicity information kept secret for 25 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd73a4018c5ff31d8465e315c911f9a580557b9b110c3b86ae8961d26a65aaa3</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T01:44:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years--591bfaa53874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-key-post-9-11-air-toxicity-information-was-kept-secret-for-25-years" /><summary type="html">New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani on Tuesday announced the release of tens of thousands of documents detailing what city officials knew about toxic air after the September 11 attacks as the 25th anniversary approaches and thousands still suffer from related illnesses.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Smithsonian chief steps down amid Trump pressure over how US history is presented</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c1df705be601c660337b921d41209501df153058ebbb3184dbb8797a7951bac</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T00:10:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure--786389f668db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-smithsonian-chief-lonnie-bunch-steps-down-amid-trump-administration-pressure" /><summary type="html">The Smithsonian announced Tuesday that Secretary Lonnie Bunch will leave his post at the end of the year as the institution faces continued scrutiny from the Trump administration over how its museums present US history.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
